I (Topi Linkala) wrote:

"I've made a patch that eliminates the confirmation for untraping if 
there is only one chest or large box on location that has no other trap. 
This way you can do #untrap > ^A ^A ^A ^A to check the chest or large 
box five times.

I think it's available from Pasi's database:

http://bilious.homelinux.org/?233

It is option driven so you can have both old and new function in same 
executable."

Now, without this patch three times cheking:

<meta>-u > y <meta>-u > y <meta>-u > y

That's 9 keystrokes.

With my patch:

<meta>-u > ^A ^A

It only takes four keystrokes.

With nine keystrokes:

<meta>-u > ^A ^A  ^A ^A ^A ^A ^A

you've checked eight times.

I'm not going to check the propability of finding a trap from a chest 
with a single untrap, but lets say it's 50%. Then three checks will 
produce 87,5% when eight will produce 99,6%.

